            "multiple": false,
            "typeClass": "primitive",
            "value": "<p>\nThis entry is a three-files data package totaling 640.95 kB containing files in .pdf and .txt formats.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nTime Coverage: The empirical material provides longitudinal coverage of songwriters’ careers, reconstructed through retrospective qualitative interviews spanning early, mid, and late career stages.\n</p>\n\n\n<p>\nIf you use this dataset, please cite: Smolka, K. (2026). <i>“I Hold On”: How Country Music Songwriters Cope with the Precarity of Craft Work — Online Appendices</i> (Version V1) [Data set]. DataverseNL.\n<a href=\" https://doi.org/10.34894/WLK4IO\" target=\" https://doi.org/10.34894/WLK4IO\"> https://doi.org/10.34894/WLK4IO</a>\n</p>"
